ITEM S4-6 — Voice: "Recognition request was cancelled" on stop
File: AITest/Views/SmartSalesVoiceView.swift

Problem: Tapping stop calls audio.stop() immediately, which abruptly kills the AVAudioEngine while SFSpeechRecognitionTask is still active. The task receives a cancellation error ("Recognition request was cancelled" — kAFAssistantErrorDomain code 203) and displays it as an error message instead of finalizing the transcript.

The UX is: record → tap stop → transcript visible → tap "Parse Sales" → analyze. The stop button is correct. The error needs to be suppressed and the flow needs to work cleanly.

Fix A — stopRecording(): call endAudio() before stopping the engine:
  private func stopRecording() {
      guard isRecording || audio.isRunning else { return }
      audio.request?.endAudio()  // Signal end-of-audio to the recognizer cleanly
      isRecording = false
      DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter(deadline: .now() + 0.3) {
          audio.stop()  // Give recognizer 300ms to finalize before engine stops
      }
  }

Fix B — In the recognition task callback, suppress the cancellation error code:
  if let callbackError {
      let nsError = callbackError as NSError
      // 216 = no speech, 203 = cancelled cleanly after endAudio() — both are non-fatal
      if nsError.domain == "kAFAssistantErrorDomain" &&
         (nsError.code == 216 || nsError.code == 203 || nsError.code == 301) { return }
      errorMessage = callbackError.localizedDescription
      stopRecording()
  }

Fix C — After recording stops with a non-empty transcript, show a brief nudge so users know what to do next. Add below the existing "Tap to record" label:
  if !transcript.isEmpty && !isRecording {
      Text("Tap \"Parse Sales\" to analyse your recording")
          .font(.caption2).foregroundColor(.secondary)
          .multilineTextAlignment(.center)
  }
  // The "Parse Sales" button already appears when !transcript.isEmpty && !isRecording — keep it as is.

