{\b ADDENDUM to ITEM 2 \emdash Save display name on first Apple Sign-Up}\par
\par
Apple only returns the user's full name on the VERY FIRST sign-in. On all subsequent\par
sign-ins, fullName fields are nil. Firebase will not retry asking Apple for it.\par
So the name must be saved to the Firebase user profile immediately.\par
\par
In the signInWithApple() method in AuthManager.swift, after the successful\par
Auth.auth().signIn(with: firebaseCredential) call, add:\par
\par
    // Save display name to Firebase profile on first Apple sign-up\par
    // Apple only provides fullName once -- save it immediately or it is lost forever\par
    if let fullName = appleCredential.fullName,\par
       let givenName = fullName.givenName \{\par
        let displayName = [givenName, fullName.familyName]\par
            .compactMap \{ $0 \}\par
            .joined(separator: " ")\par
        if !displayName.isEmpty \{\par
            let changeRequest = result.user.createProfileChangeRequest()\par
            changeRequest.displayName = displayName\par
            try? await changeRequest.commitChanges()\par
        \}\par
    \}\par
    currentUser = Auth.auth().currentUser  // refresh after profile update\par
\par
This goes directly after:\par
    let result = try await Auth.auth().signIn(with: firebaseCredential)\par
And before:\par
    currentUser = result.user\par
    isAuthenticated = true\par
\par
(Replace the "currentUser = result.user" line with "currentUser = Auth.auth().currentUser"\par
so it picks up the updated displayName after commitChanges.)\par
